      "Light for a full treadmill at 155 lb, with transport wheels",
      "16 programs and partial FTMS app connectivity",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 55-inch belt and 10 mph top speed limit it to walking and light jogging",
      "275 lb user limit, the lowest in Schwinn’s range",
      "Motor ratings conflict: 2.6 CHP in one review, 1.5 HP at a retailer; Schwinn gives none",
      "One year on parts, electronics and labour",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A sound walking treadmill at $899 for one user under 275 lb, but the SFT4.3 gives a longer belt for the same price.",
    description: "The 810 is Schwinn’s best-known treadmill. Schwinn’s US store lists a 20 by 55-inch belt, 0 to 10 mph, 0 to 10% motorized incline, a 275 lb maximum user weight, 69.1 by 35.6 by 56.7 inches assembled, 39.5 inches long folded and 155 lb, on a standard 110-120 V outlet; Garage Gym Reviews and Best Buy’s listing agree on the belt, speed, incline and capacity. Schwinn lists 10 years on the frame and drive motor and one year on mechanical parts, electronics and labour. It was $899 on 5 November 2026, in stock.",
  },
  {
    id: "schwinn-sft4-3",
    name: "Schwinn SFT4.3",
    brand: "Schwinn",
    category: "Longer Deck at the 810’s Price",
    badge: "Best Value",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FC15KY8Q?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31B3H544RJL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$899 at Schwinn Fitness on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: {"low":899,"high":899},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. running area · up to 12 mph · 0-12% motorized incline · folding · EasyDial controls",
    pros: [
      "A 60-inch running area and 12 mph for the same $899 as the 810",
      "EasyDial speed and incline controls, a fan and Bluetooth speakers",
      "Six programs and app connectivity",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Schwinn lists 325 lb; another retailer listing gives 275 lb, so check before relying on it",
      "No published motor rating",
      "One year on parts, electronics and labour",
      "Little independent review coverage",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Our pick of the four for most buyers: the 815’s deck and speed for $200 less.",
    description: "The SFT4.3 is one of Schwinn’s newer models. Schwinn’s US store lists a 20 by 60-inch running area, speeds up to 12 mph, 0 to 12% motorized incline, EasyDial controls, six programs, a 5-inch LCD with three LED windows, 76 by 34 by 57 inches assembled and 187 lb, with the same 10-year frame and motor and one-year parts, electronics and labour cover as the rest of the range. Schwinn gives a 325 lb maximum user weight, but a retailer listing in search results gave 275 lb. It was $899 on 5 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "schwinn-815",
    name: "Schwinn 815",
    brand: "Schwinn",
    category: "Top of the Range, with App Links",
    badge: "Most Features",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DNFMYCTQ?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31rZqeS4OhL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$1,099 at Schwinn Fitness on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: {"low":1099,"high":1099},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. running area · up to 12 mph · 0-12% incline · folding · Bluetooth, JRNY, Peloton and Zwift app links",
    pros: [
      "A 60-inch running area and 12 mph top speed",
      "App connectivity to JRNY, Peloton and Zwift listed by Schwinn",
      "Eight programs, Bluetooth heart-rate support and USB charging",
    ],
    cons: [
      "$200 more than the SFT4.3, which shares its frame size",
      "No motor rating from Schwinn; a deal listing called it 3 HP",
      "One year on parts, electronics and labour",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Buy it over the SFT4.3 only for the app integrations; otherwise the cheaper model gives the same deck.",
    description: "The 815 is the most expensive Schwinn treadmill. Schwinn’s US store lists a 20 by 60-inch running area, speeds up to 12 mph, 0 to 12% incline, eight programs, Bluetooth speakers and heart-rate support, USB charging and app links to JRNY, Peloton and Zwift, with a 325 lb maximum user weight, 76 by 34 by 57 inches assembled and 187 lb. A January 2026 Slickdeals listing agreed on 12 mph and 12% and described it as 3 HP. It was $1,099 on 5 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "schwinn-sft4-1",
    name: "Schwinn SFT4.1",
    brand: "Schwinn",
    category: "Cheapest Schwinn Treadmill",
    badge: "Lowest Price",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FC12V6LR?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31JTc6dgqwL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$699 at Schwinn Fitness on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: {"low":699,"high":699},
    specs: "20 x 55 in. running area · up to 10 mph · 0-10% motorized incline · 300 lb max user · compact folding",
    pros: [
      "$200 less than the 810 with similar belt, speed and incline",
      "A higher 300 lb user rating than the 810",
      "Schwinn says it assembles in 30 minutes or less",
      "Built-in fan, Bluetooth speakers and tablet holder",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Three LED windows and five programs, the plainest console in the range",
      "A 55-inch deck, short for running",
      "No published motor rating",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The better budget buy than the 810 for walking, with more capacity for less money.",
    description: "The SFT4.1 is Schwinn’s entry treadmill. Schwinn’s US store lists a 20 by 55-inch running area, speeds up to 10 mph, 0 to 10% motorized incline, a 300 lb maximum user weight, five programs, three-zone cushioning, 70 by 33 by 55 inches assembled and 180 lb, with the range’s 10-year frame and motor and one-year parts, electronics and labour cover; a retailer listing in search results agreed on the running area, speed and incline. It was $699 on 5 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "horizon-7-0-at",
    name: "Horizon 7.0 AT",
    brand: "Horizon",
    category: "Same Owner, More Treadmill",
    badge: "Step Up",
