        <div id="motors-warranty" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. The Two Things Schwinn Does Not Tell You Enough About</h2>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Motor ratings</h3>
          <p>
            None of Schwinn's four product pages gives the motor's horsepower, continuous or peak. For the 810, outside
            sources range from 1.5 HP to 2.6 CHP; for the 815, one deal listing said 3 HP. Without a manufacturer
            figure, the best guides to what each machine is built for are the <a href="/treadmill-belt-size-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>belt length</a>, top speed and user limit,
            and those point to walking and jogging, not daily running. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-horsepower-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill horsepower guide</a>
            explains why continuous ratings matter more than peak figures, if you find one.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The warranty</h3>
          <p>
            Every current Schwinn treadmill carries 10 years on the frame and drive motor and one year on mechanical
            parts, electronics and labour. The 10-year motor term is good for the price, but the one-year electronics
            term is short: console boards and motor controllers are among the parts that fail on budget treadmills, and
            after year one they are on you. Compare that with Bowflex's lifetime motor cover, or Horizon's longer parts
            terms, before deciding. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-warranty-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill warranty guide</a>
            sets out which terms matter most.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="recalls" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">6. Schwinn Treadmill Recalls</h2>
<p>
            We searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for Schwinn, Nautilus and Johnson
            Health Tech on 5 November 2026. No recall names a Schwinn treadmill. The recent Schwinn-titled recalls are
            Pacific Cycle's — electric scooters in 2021 and bicycle child carriers in 2025 — and concern the bicycle
            company, not Schwinn Fitness.
          </p>
          <p>
            The closest treadmill recall in the family is the 2022 recall of about 7,300 Nautilus T616 and T618
            treadmills sold in 2021, which can start on their own. Nautilus Inc. made those under its other brand,
            and the CPSC now says no remedy is available. If you are shopping second-hand and a seller offers a
            "Nautilus/Schwinn" treadmill, read our
            <a href="/nautilus-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Nautilus treadmills guide</a>
            to check the serial number.
          </p>
