        <div id="which" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. Which Schwinn Treadmill Should You Buy?</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>For walking on a budget:</strong> the SFT4.1 at $699. It matches the 810's belt, speed and
            incline, with a higher user rating, for $200 less.</li>
            <li><strong>For walking and some jogging:</strong> the SFT4.3 at $899. The 60-inch deck and 12 mph make it
            the most versatile Schwinn for the money.</li>
            <li><strong>For apps:</strong> the 815 at $1,099, if JRNY, Peloton or Zwift integration matters to you.</li>
            <li><strong>For the 810:</strong> buy it if you want the lightest machine (155 lb) or the one with the most
            independent coverage, and you are under 275 lb.</li>
            <li><strong>For running or more incline:</strong> step up to a Bowflex T6 or a
            <a href="/horizon-7-0-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon 7.0 AT</a>, both
            Johnson Health Tech machines with 15% incline.</li>
