        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Schwinn Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Schwinn treadmills are good value if you buy the right one for the job. These are the mistakes we see most.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the 810 to run on</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Its 55-inch belt and 10 mph top speed suit walking and light jogging. If you plan to run, the SFT4.3 costs the same and gives a 60-inch deck and 12 mph.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the user limit</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The 810 is rated to 275 lb, the lowest in the range, and one retailer gives the SFT4.3 the same figure against Schwinn’s 325 lb. Leave a margin below the limit, especially for running.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the 10-year warranty covers everything</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">It covers the frame and drive motor. Parts, electronics and labour are covered for one year. A failed console board in year two is a paid repair.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying $1,099 for features you will not use</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The 815 and SFT4.3 share a deck, frame and speed. The $200 difference buys app integrations and two more programs; if you will not use JRNY, Peloton or Zwift, buy the SFT4.3.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

